From 6c51d37726ede8a0b619b1ba49c45e8ac7fc34ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR-Vensuki <260785366+LR-Vensuki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:27:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Legacy iOS: memory watcher, no GPU drawing from the
 background

Every 2 s a background thread measures the free address space below the
shared cache and iOS's memory level (kern.memorystatus_level). When
either gets low Gecko gets memory pressure; near the point where iOS
kills the app, or the GPU driver finds no hole for its 16 MB blocks,
the embedding app is told (LegacyFoxMemoryCritical).

iOS kills an app that sends the GPU commands from the background: the
SWGL GPU path pauses there, and entering the background waits for a
frame already begun.

LF_SWGL_GPU_STATS also logs frame rate, drawing time and pixels drawn
every 2 s, malloc zones, and GPU textures of 8 MB or more.
